final_message:
I wrote the workflow document. I couldn't render it here (no LibreOffice), so I haven't confirmed it fits 2–3 pages. It has about 1,560 words in compact 9pt text, which should land at roughly three pages.

The document covers:
- the end-to-end steps, owners and decision gates;
- the modular quotation structure, built as a five-level tree: lamp assembly, feature modules, design elements, child parts, raw material;
- three change classes for post-nomination design changes (A, B, C) with their approvals;
- the flexibility points;
- requirements for the TechSol platform;
- assumptions and open items.

**Price change approval conflict.** The assignment text, a revision-3 proposal and the working notes say Purchase alone approves price change requests. The governing record, approved 19-Oct-2026, requires Finance controllers, Program Managers and Purchase, all three. The revision-3 proposal dates from 22-Oct and is unapproved, and the decision register says a later date doesn't give it authority. So I designed for three approvers. The document recommends that the platform keep the approver list configurable, so the CPO can decide on Purchase-only without a rebuild.

**Not invented.** The cost thresholds that separate change classes, any CPO sign-off limit, review time targets and the expected delay saving aren't in the records. They are listed as open items for the CPO to decide. I also assumed that TRSO updates keep the existing signatories (ER, Quality, Purchase), and flagged that for confirmation.

Files are in outputs/:
- Lamp_Sourcing_Nomination_Workflow_Draft.docx

DONE
